From 8a022165598c81dd377cb194acd9278c1df9c6fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:28:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Blu-ray] Show the HAVi background plane and a BD-J screen
 that plays no playlist

The Kodi side of libbluray-9070 (SamuriHL's libbluray patch 07), which draws the
HAVi background plane of BD-J discs and adds bd_bdj_waiting_for_playback().

The background plane. libbluray delivers it through the ARGB overlay callback
on plane 2 (BD_OVERLAY_BG). The callback took only planes 0 and 1, and any
CLOSE closed all of them: a disc that sets its background colour to
transparent would have wiped its own menu. Now:
- plane 2 is kept with the others, and a CLOSE closes its own plane (the whole
  composition when nothing is left, as before);
- the composition goes back to front: background, PG, IG;
- the background lies behind the video and the overlays are drawn over it, so
  it is shown only while no playlist is open (hidden on BD_EVENT_PLAYLIST and
  when a video stream opens, shown when BD-J waits with no playlist). With
  full-screen video, which is all libbluray presents (it does not implement
  BD-J video scaling), that is exactly what a player composites;
- a flush that carries the background alone does not count as menu graphics
  (IsInMenu()), and an IG close that leaves only the background ends them.
The planes are now changed under a lock of their own: the BD-J callbacks run
on the JVM's graphics thread and the background is re-posted from the player
thread. m_hasOverlay, read by the player and the GUI, is atomic.

A BD-J screen with no playlist (a disc's own resume prompt, John Wick 3).
bd_read() has nothing to give then, and the demuxer probe kept the player
thread in the input stream's idle loop: no player message was handled, the
streams never became ready, the busy dialog took every key and nothing was
drawn, because disc overlays are drawn only with a decoded picture. Now:
- Prepare() does not open the demuxer while the disc waits
  (GetBdjWaitState()), and the main loop keeps running and opens it once the
  disc starts a playlist; a resume position is not applied then (logged);
- once the disc has kept menu graphics up with no playlist for 3 s (a normal
  BD-J start draws a logo first), playback start is announced: busy dialog
  gone, fullscreen video window, keys to the disc; HasVideo() says so;
- with no video configured, the render manager draws the latest disc menu
  composition by itself, full screen, in the fullscreen video window only
  (SetDiscMenuWithoutPicture(), OVERLAY::CRenderer::NO_PICTURE, a slot after
  the render buffers). A video stream ends it.

Not covered: a screen with no playlist that a BD-J title shows after its video
played (the demuxer is open then and the read idles as before).

Design from SamuriHL's coreelec-xbmc 54b2c4bec6ff, commits bfa8ea9bd559 and
6ad6c5edd48d (read as data; SHA256 of the patches kept with the sources of the
change): the deferred demuxer, the wait state with its event drain, the 3 s
menu-only start, SignalStreamsReady() and SetBackgroundVisible() are his,
adapted to this VideoPlayer. His drawing without a picture relies on a
presentation-time overlay composition this tree does not have; here it is a
slot of its own in the overlay renderer. The overlay lock, the IsInMenu() rule
and the per-plane close are written again for this tree.

Co-developed-by: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
